# Git Commit Messages

When generating commit messages, follow Conventional Commits specification:
- Use prefixes: feat:, fix:, docs:, chore:, refactor:, test:, perf:, ci:, style:
- Keep the entire message under 60 characters
- Use lowercase for the type prefix
- Use imperative mood (e.g., "add" not "added")

# Code Style Conventions

## Modularity (STRICT)
- Files: Max 150 lines
- Functions: Max 30 lines
- Classes: Max 200 lines

## Before Writing New Code
- Always search codebase first for existing types/utilities
- Inherit/extend existing types (Pick, Omit, Partial)
- Check types/, utils/, constants/ folders

## Export Patterns
- Never use `export default` - always named exports
- Never use index.ts barrel files - import directly from source

## Type Safety
- Never cast with `any` or `unknown`
- Never use `as Type` casting
- Use type guards instead

## Post-Implementation
- Run: npm test, npx tsc --noEmit, npm run lint, npm run build
- Fix ALL errors before considering task complete
